  "question": {
    "text": "An object is projected from the earth's surface with escape velocity at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mn>0</mn><mo>°</mo></math> with horizontal. What is the angle made by the velocity with horizontal when the object reaches a height <math> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow> </math> from the earth's surface? <math> <mi>R</mi> </math> is the radius of the earth. Horizontal can be considered as a line parallel to the tangent at the earth's surface just below the object."
